From aa7eafbc2750b6a4e4a9dec56cb846c5a9429d01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:23:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native token index (token DB, token-id group,
 mempool tokens)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port chronik-db io/token/{data,batch,io}.rs (token_tx, token_meta and
token_genesis_info tables, batch validation with cycle detection),
groups/token_id.rs (token-id history and UTXOs in the eCash-tier dup
encoding: outpoint ‖ sats LE8 ‖ raw script) and mem/tokens.rs as the
Mempool's token hook, with the Rust error texts.

Rust reads the committed DB while a block is written; the native writer
reads through the block's write transaction, so the mint-vault genesis
lookup ignores tx nums of the batch being written, which reproduces the
Rust result (test_batch_vault fails otherwise).

Encodings are checked against Rust: a second test-only exporter,
chronik-db/tests/export_native_db_values.rs, run on the eCash-tier
crate, writes 77 golden DB values (blocks, txs, block stats, spent-by,
history pages and merge operands, UTXO dups, metadata, TokenMeta,
GenesisInfo, DbTokenTx) that the native code must decode and re-encode
byte-exactly.

Tests: all 12 Rust tests of these modules plus 26 native cases and the
13 golden cases.

Tier: eCash
